⍝ lib/set.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 10: sets as characteristic functions α → 𝔹 (a set is the test of its membership)
∈ ∶ α → (α → 𝔹) → 𝔹
∈ ξ η ≔ (η ξ)
∅ˢ ∶ α → 𝔹
∅ˢ ξ ≔ ⊥
𝕌 ∶ α → 𝔹
𝕌 ξ ≔ ⊤
∪ ∶ (α → 𝔹) → (α → 𝔹) → (α → 𝔹)
∪ ξ η θ ≔ (∨ (ξ θ) (η θ))
∩ ∶ (α → 𝔹) → (α → 𝔹) → (α → 𝔹)
∩ ξ η θ ≔ (∧ (ξ θ) (η θ))
∖ ∶ (α → 𝔹) → (α → 𝔹) → (α → 𝔹)
∖ ξ η θ ≔ (∧ (ξ θ) (¬ (η θ)))
∁ ∶ (α → 𝔹) → (α → 𝔹)
∁ ξ θ ≔ (¬ (ξ θ))
⍝ the finite set of the elements of a list (membership by ≐), and the members of a set among the elements of a list
setof ∶ 𝔏 ℚ[i] → (ℚ[i] → 𝔹)
setof ξ θ ≔ (elem θ ξ)
members ∶ (α → 𝔹) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
members ≔ filter
